Now I have sufficient independent verification data. Let me compile the full assessment.

**Key findings from independent research:**

1. **SWE-bench-Live data confirmed**: 1,890 instances / 223 repos (May 2026 current figure) ✓; Agentless baseline numbers (11.67% GPT-4o, 12.00% GPT-4.1, 13.33% DeepSeek V3) confirmed from Table 3 of arXiv 2505.23419 ✓; NeurIPS 2025 D&B status confirmed ✓

2. **Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B confirmed**: 30.5B total / ~3.3B active, MoE, 128 experts, released July 2025, code-specialized ✓

3. **SpecRover 107/207 (51.7%) claim re-verified**: Independently confirmed via direct WebFetch of arXiv HTML — Section V-A "Reasons for Failure" explicitly documents this statistic ✓

4. **Agent-CoEvo confirmed**: Real paper, real design (coevolving code + test patches), outperforms agentless baselines — properly addressed in Round 5 ✓

5. **"Officially-abandoned SWE-bench Verified"**: Factually accurate — OpenAI's Feb 2026 announcement confirmed abandonment, but OpenAI recommends SWE-bench Pro (not SWE-bench-Live) as the replacement. The phrasing in the proposal conflates abandonment with endorsing SWE-bench-Live as the successor.

6. **Round 4 unresolved issues**: All three flagged items (EMNLP scope inconsistency, Verified framing, 0.65 threshold) remain unaddressed in Round 5.

